# Relative imports

Write relative imports without a `.js` suffix. Keep `.js` only when the imported file is JavaScript, such as `svelte.config.js`.

```ts
import { createHueClient } from './client';
import type { HueClient } from './client';
import config from './svelte.config.js';
```

`@huxel/client` and `@huxel/app` use `"moduleResolution": "bundler"`. `NodeNext` rejects extensionless relative imports, so do not switch those packages back. `vp pack` adds `.js` again in published `dist` files.

`bun run check` fails while relative `.js` imports of TypeScript files remain. Update them with `bun run codemod`.
